      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- South Ro 2.0 [zone=43]\n**Who:**\n- Ruwakka [ _Raid Recruiter_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 65\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Expedition\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Loot\n**Related Zones:**\n- Deepest Guk: The Curse Reborn (Raid) [zone=448]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Chest of the Foci [npc=27909]\n- Energy Focus [npc=30464]\n- Executioner Gimdk [npc=25272]\n- Gimdk`s chest [npc=27910]\n- Matter Focus [npc=30465]\n- Scout Granos [npc=25271]\n- Scout Mainil [npc=25270]\n- Spirit Focus [npc=30466]\n- The First Witness [npc=30463]\n- The Slimy Chest of the Witness [npc=27911]\n**Era:** | !Lost Dungeons of Norrath\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Raid\n**Min. # of Players:** | 6\n**Max. # of Players:** | 54\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Oct 26 16:50:45 2006\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | _This raid expedition begins with Ruwakka in the Wayfarer camp of South Ro._\nYou say, 'Hail, Ruwakka'\nRuwakka says 'Me helping de adventurers of de Wayfarers Brotherhood. Me in charge of recruiting brave fighters for de strange stuff going on in de land of de froggies. If you rally de call of your friends we needs help wit dis serious [problem].'\nYou say, 'What problem?'\nRuwakka says 'We learned from de scouts that de First Witness of de Cauldron of Hate found a way to harness de foul curse in Deepest Guk. De First Witness is de strongest of them all. He amassing a group of followers large enough to make him deity! We needs you to stop de First Witness 'fore he unleash fury on us all. Are you [interested]?'\nYou say, 'I am interested.'\nRuwakka smashes his left fist into his right palm, for effect. 'Crush de First Witness and all of dem followers!'\nDeepest Guk: The Curse Reborn is now available to you.\n_The entrance to the instance is located in Innothule Swamp at the tree like other LDoNs. Note, this expedition takes a long time to load, at least 5 minutes. If you click too soon, you get sent to the Succor location._\n\n---\n\n_In summary:_\n_Part of the raid follows Scout Mainil through to the northwest room (the prison) while the other part of the raid stays with Scout Granos and protects him from spawning mobs._\n_Once Mainil is in the jail, raid members can kill the risen acolytes that spawn alongside the Executioner. If you do not kill the risen acolytes before they get executed, they turn into wisps which in turn spawn as adds in the final encounter._\n_Also at this time, Granos begins his own trek through the zone. He'll head to the northeast room (the cauldron room). Once he reaches it, kill the three \"\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ Focus\" mobs (one in front of the cauldron; two in either attached room) and then The First Witness. Chests spawn with loot after The First Witness's death._\n\n---\n\n_In detail:_\nTwo froglok scouts stand at the zone-in:\nYou say, 'Hail, Scout Granos'\nScout Granos says 'Greetings, it is good that you came to assist us. We cannot allow the First Witness of Hate to complete his spell. Half of you are going to have to go ahead with my companion, while the other half are going to need to wait here with me. We suspect that the First Witness will attempt to send a force here as a diversion. We will be able to catch up with them soon'\nYou say, 'Hail, Scout Mainil'\nScout Mainil says 'Greetings friend, thank you for making such haste to get here. The situation is worse than we feared. Not only is the First Witness attempting to complete his spell, he has minions that he is sending to the outside. He is hoping that by assaulting Gukta he will distract us. My friend here will help you guard the exit, please ensure that nothing happens to him. I'll be talking half of you with me, so we can assess the situation. As soon as I have a better idea of what is going on, I will pass on more instructions to you. When you are [ready] please let me know, and we shall be off.'\nYou say, 'We are ready.'\nScout Mainil says 'Ok, half of you please accompany me while we scout ahead. Granos, I will let you know when I know more.'\n_Part of your raid needs to follow and protect Scout Mainil as he walks through the zone to the northwest room (the Foreboding Prison). The other part of the raid should stay with Scout Granos. Mobs will spawn in waves of two and attack him._\n_Note: Don't attack the Scouts._\nScout Mainil says '\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ this is not productive to our goal. I will not stand here and be attacked by those who came to assist me! If this does not stop, I will be forced to vacate. Regardless of the consequences.'\nShortly into the trek...\nScout Mainil says 'It sounds as though the assault has begun. I hope that Granos and your companions can hold the entrance.' He then studies the ground, 'It appears as though we are on the right track. We are making excellent time so far.'\nA short time later...\nScout Mainil says, 'Hmm, this is very unusual. There seems to be a second path leading off to the North. It appears as though someone may be assisting the first witness. I will need to follow this second set of prints to investigate further.' He then scratches a note into the boulder before him with instructions for his partner.\nThe scout appears to no longer need your protection.\nUpon entering the jail area...\nScout Mainil says 'This is worse than I feared. The Executioner is feeding those souls to the Cauldron to assist the First Witness. I fear that your friends may have more to deal with than just those that are assisting with his spell. It appears the Executioner is protected by the same magic that guards the First Witness of Hate. All we will be able to do is stem the flow of Souls from this place, aside from that, your friends will be on their own.'\nIn that room, the executioner summons a \"frog risen\":\nExecutioner Gimdk focuses his attention on a new Risen, 'The Cauldron shall feast on your essence!'\nIf you manage to kill the frog risen before he's absorbed, the event will continue. If you fail:\nThe Risen before the Executioner explodes, leaving a small bit of dancing energy where it once stood.\n...And an unattackable wisp appears and heads to the northeast room, respawning as an add.\n_Part of the raid can remain and keep killing the risen acolytes as they spawn while the rest of the raid follows the now-mobile Scout Granos (if acolytes are left alive for the Executioner to kill, wisps continue to spawn from their deaths)._\n_The Executioner becomes attackable once the three foci are killed over by the cauldron (more on the foci mobs to follow)._\n\n---\n\n_Scout Granos begins walking through the zone. His destination is the far northeast room. Once there..._\nScout Granos says 'There are the foci. They must be destroyed before he completes his spell, or his power will increase tenfold.'\n_You'll see a giant cauldron, above which is The First Witness. You'll also see numerous adds in the room and an evil eye called \"Energy Focus\". This evil eye, along with the Matter Focus and Spirit Focus in the attached rooms must be killed (failing to do so will cause the final boss's strength to power up significantly)._\n_Adds spawn throughout the event. None of the named mobs have any special melee abilities. There is no rampaging, flurrying, or enraging. The evil eyes hit for a max ~1,400 while The First Witness hits for a max ~1,650._\n_Energy Focus casts two spells:_\nBlurring Focus: NPC Hatelist 400', Chromatic (-150)\n1: Decrease Spell Haste by 50%\n2: Decrease ATK by 200\n3: Cancel Magic(9)\n4: Cancel Magic(9)\n5: Limit: Combat Skills Not Allowed\nLife Vortex: NPC Hatelist 400', Disease (-250)\n1: Increase Disease Counter by 38\n2: Decrease Hitpoints by 600 per tick\n_Matter Focus casts two spells:_\nEverlasting Essence: Self 0', Unresistable (0)\n1: Increase Chance to Reflect Spell by 60%\nSwirling Matter: NPC Hatelist 400', Prismatic (-200)\n1: Stun(8.00 sec)\n_Spirit Focus casts one spell:_\nInfinite Mass: NPC Hatelist 400', Prismatic (-200)\n1: Increase Curse Counter by 24\n2: Decrease Movement by 65%\n3: Decrease Mana by 200 per tick\n\n---\n\nEnergy Focus has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nYour faction standing with Servants of the First Witness got worse.\nYou gained raid experience!\nMatter Focus has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nYour faction standing with Servants of the First Witness got worse.\nYou gained raid experience!\nSpirit Focus has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nYour faction standing with Servants of the First Witness got worse.\nYou gained raid experience!\nAs the last Focus blinks lifelessly, the room trembles. The First Witness screams as his shield of protection fails, 'Infidels! I was so close! You shall die!'\nYour victory has weakened a shroud of magic cloaking the dungeon's treasure.\n_Once the three evil eyes are dead, kill The First Witness (a straight melee encounter)._\nThe First Witness has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nYour faction standing with Servants of the First Witness got worse.\nYou gained raid experience!\nYour victory has shattered the shroud of magic surrounding the dungeon's treasure\nThe First Witness screams silently as his magic fails. You feel a wave of hate wash over you, as a voice whispers in your head, 'There will always be a First. You have not won.'\n_Three chests spawn around the area with loot._\n\n---\n\n_Known raid loot from this event (Two items per chest, can receive duplicates):_\nChest of the Foci\nCauldron-Cursed Shard of Power\nFocus Stone of Enhanced Protection\nGloves of the Cauldron Cursed\nMossy Enchanted Stone\nSlime-Soaked Jewel\nThe Slimy Chest of the Witness\nEnchanted Gem of the Scout\nEnchanted Orb of Spirit\nFocus Shard of Enhanced Protection\nGem of Focused Rage\nGlowing Stone of Agility\nKnave's Slime-Soaked Chestplate\nGimdk's Chest\nAbjuration Stone of Focus\nEnchanted Orb 