      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- South Ro 2.0 [zone=43]\n**Who:**\n- Friggal Bribbitz [ _Raid Recruiter_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 65\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Expedition\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Loot\n**Related Zones:**\n- Deepest Guk: Ritualist of Hate (Raid) [zone=559]\n- Innothule Swamp 2.0 [zone=6]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Bidip`s Ornate Chest [npc=27903]\n- Cursed Keepers` Slimy Chest [npc=27901]\n- Gragna the Cursed [npc=27944]\n- Gragna`s Worn Chest [npc=27904]\n- Leklos the Bonekeeper [npc=27942]\n- Leklos` Bonepile [npc=27902]\n- The Cavern Creeper [npc=27941]\n- The Cursed Keeper [npc=27945]\n- The Cursed Spore [npc=27943]\n**Era:** | !Lost Dungeons of Norrath\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Raid\n**Min. # of Players:** | 6\n**Max. # of Players:** | 54\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Jan 1 22:33:34 2008\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | _This raid expedition begins with Friggal Bribbitz at the Wayfarer camp in South Ro. You must have at least six players in your raid and no more than 54._\nYou say, 'Hail, Friggal Bribbitz'\nFriggal Bribbitz says 'With the help of the Wayfarer's Brotherhood and adventurers like you, we hope to stop the Witnesses of Hate from completing their dark rituals and cursing all those who have entered Deepest Guk. If you can rally the call of your friends perhaps you can help us with a serious [problem].'\nYou say, 'What problem?'\nFriggal Bribbitz says 'We have been hearing reports that the Witnesses of Hate are amassing sacrifices for a dark ritual. Lich Rtrangi appears to be behind the sacrifices with the intent to afflict the living Frogloks with a disfiguring curse. We have a scout who can assist you in Deepest Guk with infiltrating Rtangi's domain and putting a stop to his plans. Are you [interested]?'\nYou say, 'I am interested'\nFriggal Bribbitz says 'The scout will meet you inside Deepest Guk. Be safe, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.'\n_You are assigned the expedition \"Deepest Guk: Ritualist of Hate\"._\n_The entrance to the zone is located in Innothule Swamp at +940, +570, 16. (Your compass will indicate direction.)_\n_In the instance you will have to kill five named mobs in order (one spawns after the other in different parts of the zone): Leklos the Bonekeeper, The Cavern Creeper, The Cursed Spore, Gragna the Cursed, and The Cursed Keeper._\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Deepest Guk: Ritualist of Hate.\n_Trash here are around 65-66th level, hit for ~1,400 and respawn._\n\n---\n\n_One of the first rooms you enter will have several warriors of Gukta battling undead. In the next room is Leklos the Bonekeeper._\nWarrior of Gukta says, Thank you for your hasty assistance brave travellers. Leklos lies within this room. We shall hold his minions back while you destroy him.\nWarrior of Gukta shouts 'Back you spawn of evil, the warriors of Gukta shall always prevail.'\nLeklos the Bonekeeper says 'None shall defy the will of the keeper.'\n_Leklos hits for a max ~2,300; enrages; and casts two spells:_\nBone Whirl: PB AE 250', Magic (-300)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 600\n2: Stun(6.00 sec/65)\nFlesh Pile: PB AE 250', Magic (-500)\n1: Decrease ATK by 300\n2: Decrease AC by 90\n3: Decrease HP when cast by 300\nLeklos the Bonekeeper has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nYour faction standing with Innoruuk's Curse of the Cauldron got worse.\nLeklos the Bonekeeper's corpse falls to the ground a lifeless pile of bones.\nA Warrior of Gukta says, 'Thank you for the help adventurers, but you must hurry deeper into the cavern. Some of our resident Evokers are trying to take care of a cursed creature that ambushed some of us on the way down. I am sure they could use your help. Please listen for chanting and you should find them easily. We shall make our way back to Gukta and report to the others what is going on.'\n\n---\n\n_Next up is The Cavern Creeper, which you will encounter a little ways further in the dungeon._\nYou hear the sound of chanting coming from deeper within the dungeon, an invisible force seems to be pulling you east.\nMaster Evoker of Gukta says, 'You must hurry, I thought we could handle this with just the four of us so we told the others to go on ahead but the ritual has taken so much out of me that we are barely managing to contain that creature in the room. We need your help, if you can distract it my apprentices may be able to complete the ritual which will cut off its source of dark power.'\n_Past the Master Evoker you will find the Cavern Creeper._\nThe Cavern Creeper lunges out with its spiked tendrils, focusing on its prey.\n_It hits for a max ~2,800; AE rampages for full damage; enrages; and casts two spells:_\nFist of Innoruuk: Single Target, Magic (-500)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 5000\n2: Stun(12.00 sec)\n3: Feign Death\nPoisoned Barbs of the Cavern: PB AE 250', Poison (-350)\n1: Decrease HP when cast by 500\n2: Decrease Hitpoints by 500 per tick\n3: Drunk if Alcohol Tolerance not at least 50\n4: Increase Poison Counter by 36\nThe Cavern Creeper has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nYour faction standing with Innoruuk's Curse of the Cauldron got worse.\nYou hear the sound of something breaking open as the giant beast falls to the ground lifeless.\nOne of the Evoker's shakes his head once and then says, 'Thank you for your assistance my friends. Some of our Shamans have made their way to the north in an effort to contain another of the Keeper's evil minions. Please head to the north and listen for voices this should help you find them. We will head back to Gukta and report on your progress. The Master Evoker will stay and help when he can.'\nYour victory has weakened a shroud of magic cloaking the dungeon's treasure.\n\n---\n\n_Your next target is The Cursed Spore._\nWhispers of several voices can be heard from straight ahead.\n_You will come across several Prophets of Gukta who've surrounded The Cursed Spore._\nThe Cursed Spore says 'You come to destroy the master so I must destroy you instead.'\n_It hits for a max ~2,900; enrages; and casts two spells:_\nCursed Keeper's Siphon: PB AE 400', Disease (-275)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 500 per tick\n2: Decrease Mana by 300 per tick\n3: Increase Disease Counter by 45\nTrance of Innoruuk: Single Target, Magic (-500)\n1: Mesmerize(2/65)\n_Throughout the fight you'll see emotes indicating resistances have been lowered:_\nA blue light engulfs the Prophets as they summon forth the power of Mithaniel reducing the Cursed Spore's inherent resistance to changes in its attack speed. Prophet of Gukta says, 'The ritual has been a slight success. We have broken through one of this cursed beings immunities. Try reducing its attack speed while we prepare for the next part of the ritual.'\nA blue light engulfs the Prophets as they summon forth the power of Mithaniel reducing all of The Cursed Spore's inherent resistances slightly. Prophet of Gukta says, 'Keep it up everyone, because of the damage you have done we were able to force another weakness upon it. You should be able to cast a little more effectively now but we will need more time before we can increase your effectiveness.'\nA blue light engulfs the Prophets as they summon forth the power of Mithaniel significantly reducing all of The Cursed Spore's inherent resistances. Prophet of Gukta says, 'Excellent, we have reduced his resistance to all magical abilities even more, keep distracting him while we prepare for the final part of the ritual.'\nA blue light engulfs the Prophets as they summon forth the power of Mithaniel completely removing all of The Cursed Spore's inherent resistances. Prophet of Gukta says, 'The ritual is complete and we have been very successful. His ability to resist your magic should be almost nonexistent.'\nThe Cursed Spore has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nYour faction standing with Innoruuk's Curse of the Cauldron got worse.\nThe Cursed Spore's corpse falls to the ground no longer capable of moving on its own.\nProphet of Gukta says, 'Your assistance has helped turn the tide of battle, but it is not over yet. The Cursed Keeper knows you are here and he has sent more minions to hinder your progress. You must continue on as time is running short. Four of our clerics and a paladin have run ahead to take care of the kidnapper Gragna but they will need your help. Listen for his voice and you should be able to find him. We will return to Gukta and make a report on your progress.'\n\n---\n\n_Next up is Gragna the Cursed._\nYou hear a voice from the south. Knight of Gukta shouts, 'Please noble adventurers hurry to me, our time is running short.'\nKnight of Gukta says, 'You have arrived just in time. We have managed to confine this cursed being to this room but for some reason are unable to affect it in any other way. The only help I can offer is by granting the blessing of Mithaniel to those I feel need it while you are fighting the beast.'\nGragna the Cursed says 'The curse has gifted me with many abilities, come let me show you the way to the underworld.'\n_He hits for a max ~2,900; enrages; and casts three spells:_\nAssail of Innoruuk: PB AE 300', Magic (-500)\n1: Decrease Magic Resist by 100\n2: Decrease Fire Resist by 100\n3: Decrease Cold Resist by 100\n4: Decrease Poison Resist by 100\n5: Decrease Disease Resist by 100\nPact of Innoruuk: Single Target, Prismatic (-275)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 1000\nScorch of Innoruuk: PB AE 300', Prismatic (-275)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 3000\n_During the fight, the tank may be healed by the Paladin Guktans (spell \"Mithaniel's Blessing\"):_\nThe four healers begin to glow increasing the power of the Paladin. Knight of Gukta says, 'Oh great Mithaniel please bless these great fighters with your healing touch.'\nGragna the Cursed has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nYour faction standing with Innoruuk's Curse of the Cauldron got worse.\nGragna's decayed corpse falls to the floor as the taint from the curse drains from her body to reveal her true visage\nKnight of Gukta says 'Thank you for your help, we shall return to Gukta and report your progress.'\nYour victory has weakened a shroud of magic cloaking the dungeon's treasure.\nAs the final blow is struck an angry voice fills the halls. The Cursed Keeper says, 'You meddlesome fools, you have ruined my plans, but I shall have my retribution. Come to me if you dare and I will show you the glory of everlasting pain.'\nYou hear the voice of the master evoker in your mind, 'Your efforts have paid off, we have stopped him from accomplishing his plans and now we must ask that you destroy him while he is weak. Please make haste to the back of the dungeon and rescue our brethren.'\n\n---\n\n_Finally, you will encounter The Cursed Keeper._\nAn evil aura calls to you from the left.\n_The Cursed Keeper hits for a max ~2,900; AE rampages for full damage (does NOT enrage); and casts five spells:_\nAllure of Hatred: Single Target, Magic (-500)\n1: Charm up to level 65\n2: Increase ATK by 100\n3: Increase Damage Shield by 50\n4: Spell-Damage Shield(-250)\n5: Increase Attack Speed by 25%\nCursed Keeper's Anger: PB AE 400', Prismatic (-200)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 750 per tick\nCursed Keeper's Force: PB AE 400', Magic (-250)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 100\nCursed Keeper's Hatred: PB AE 400', Chromatic (-200)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 750 per tick\n2: Decrease Mana by 600 per tick\nStrike of Innoruuk: PB AE 400', Magic (-500)\n1: Decrease Fire Resist by 200\n2: Decrease Cold Resist by 200\n3: Decrease Magic Resist by 200\n4: Decrease Poison Resist by 200\n5: Decrease Disease Resist by 200\n6: Increase Curse Counter by 50\nThe Cursed Keeper has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nYour faction standing with Innoruuk's Curse of the Cauldron got worse.\nYour victory has shattered the shroud of magic surrounding the dungeon's treasure\nBidip Moktu stands up and shakes his head in an effort to regain his senses. Realizing that he has been saved he cheers looks at you all and salutes. Bidip Moktu says, 'Thank you so much for saving me. Please take this chest as a token of my gratitude.'\n_Up to Four chests with loot spawn around Bidip Moktu._\n\n---\n\n_Known raid loot from this event (Two items from Bidip`s Chest, Two items from Cursed Keeper`s Chest, One item from Gragna`s chest, one item from Leklos` Bonepile, can receive duplicates from same chest):_\nLeklos` Bonepile\nGlowing Stone of Frozen Slime\nGlowing Stone of Precision\nHeretic's Hood of Darkness\nOoze-Covered Stone\nGragna`s Worn Chest\nRitualist's Stone of Flowing Health\nRitualist's Stone of Rage\nSlime-Coated Crusader's Gem\nSlime-Coated Shard of Hate\nBidip`s Ornate Chest\nEnchanted Stone of Burning Rage\nRitualist's Gem of Power\nShard of Eternal Pain\nShard of the Cursed Mind\nCursed Keepers` Slimy Chest\nBurning Acid Shard\nRitualist's Divination Gem\nRitualist's Orb of Enhanced Protection\nSlime Covered Stone of Life\n\n---\n\nEp57 Ritualist of Hate LDoN Raid EverQuest TLP Mangler - YouTube\nTap to unmute\nEp57 Ritualist of Hate LDoN Raid EverQuest TLP Mangler Ion Blaze Gaming\nIon Blaze Gaming11.5K subscribers\nWatch on\n- Burning Acid Shard [item=61255]\n- Enchanted Stone of Burning Rage [item=72993]\n- Glowing Stone of Frozen Slime [item=51035]\n- Glowing Stone of Precision [item=72909]\n- Heretic's Hood of Darkness [item=72873]\n- Ooze-Covered Stone [item=73353]\n- Ritualist's Divination Gem [item=61256]\n- Ritualist's Gem of Power [item=61254]\n- Ritualist's Orb of Enhanced Protection [item=72906]\n- Ritualist's Stone of Flowing Health [item=72995]\n- Ritualist's Stone of Rage [item=72908]\n- Shard of Eternal Pain [item=59768]\n- Shard of the Cursed Mind [item=72907]\n- Slime Covered Stone of Life [item=72994]\n- Slime-Coated Crusader's Gem [item=64157]\n- Slime-Coated Shard of Hate [item=60063]",
